opinions={
'ARI@LAR':('Rams passing with a concentrated Arizona response','Stafford with Nacua or Adams; McBride or Michael Wilson coming back. Arizona target concentration is more compelling than chasing an interchangeable bargain WR.','ARI trade news says Harrison was dealt to Houston; current boxes show Wilson/McBride heavy targets. Nacua has sparse observed games, so his mean is selection-sensitive.','A pass-led Rams lead can create Arizona comeback attempts, aligning QB and receivers across both sides. A single average cannot encode that joint story; the missing Sunday baseline prevents measuring disagreement.','Rams quick separation and a rushing finish can kill the full-game stack; Brissett pressure/turnovers can make attempts unproductive.','LAR','passing_volume',1.10,['Matthew Stafford','Puka Nacua','Davante Adams','Trey McBride','Michael Wilson']),
'BAL@CLE':('Henry first; quarterback identity decides the passing alternative','Derrick Henry is the cleaner Baltimore opportunity story than assuming Lamar starts. Judkins deserves reinspection after the Browns backup transaction.','Henry has three recent observed games near 24 carries; official Ravens Week 5 material identifies Huntley. Browns Oct13 news places Raheim Sanders on IR. None establishes Week 6 starter/redistribution.','Baltimore sustaining drives through Henry can increase team carries without requiring a passing shootout; Cleveland backup loss might concentrate touches but cannot justify an unsupported numeric transfer.','A Jackson return changes rushing and scoring allocation; Cleveland front quality and a low-possession game can cap yardage. Do not infer easy matchup from individual injured linemen.','BAL','rushing_volume',1.10,['Derrick Henry','Lamar Jackson','Tyler Huntley','Quinshon Judkins']),
'BUF@LV':('Allen ceiling with Bowers response; keep Cook control alternative','Allen plus one receiver is more attractive than automatically doubling a diffuse Bills receiving tree; Bowers is the most coherent receiving response. Cook remains a competing game-control branch.','Observed Cook carries exceed twenty in the recent window while Bills receiver targets are spread. Raiders news identifies Mendoza debut and Jeanty/receiver uncertainties from prior-week reporting; Bills listed Moore inactive Monday.','If Las Vegas forces sustained Buffalo scoring, passing volume and a Bowers response travel together. If Bills lead easily, Cook volume can replace passing opportunity.','Allen rushing/TD production can win without two receivers. Cousins/Mendoza split risk, Jeanty health and Buffalo OL status must be refreshed; Monday overtime totals should not be treated as Sunday expectation.','BUF','passing_volume',1.10,['Josh Allen','Khalil Shakir','James Cook III','Brock Bowers','Kirk Cousins','Fernando Mendoza']),
'CAR@PHI':('Carolina is a live response; avoid old Eagles-star assumptions','Young–McMillan deserves a real comparison against Hurts with currently available pass catchers; Wicks/Lemon are research targets, not declared values.','CAR official news records bye rest and starting CBs Horn/Mike Jackson on IR. PHI Oct13 official discussion concerns operating without Barkley/Smith and young OL; Bigsby IR appears in team news.','Carolina sustaining drives can keep Philadelphia passing; Eagles personnel turnover can concentrate or fragment replacement opportunity. Opponent CB absences alone do not prove easy passing.','Philadelphia defensive pressure, uncertain Coker health and replacement offense quality may stop the mutual-scoring story. Barkley/Smith return would materially change it.','CAR','passing_volume',1.10,['Bryce Young','Tetairoa McMillan','Jalen Hurts','Dontayvion Wicks','Makai Lemon','Saquon Barkley','DeVonta Smith']),
'CHI@ATL':('Bijan continuity over a premature quarterback shootout','Bijan with a Chicago receiver is the initial lean; full Williams–London stacks are a separate branch contingent on actual quarterback health.','Bijan has substantial observed carries/targets; Bears Oct9 report said Williams questionable after hamstring absence and Monangai out for Week 5. Atlanta primary coverage notes Penix ribs uncertainty.','With unstable quarterbacks, Atlanta can lean on running and short throws. Bijan production does not automatically imply Penix or two Atlanta receivers hit ceilings.','Brian Robinson retains meaningful observed carries, and a healthy Williams can force a different pace. Prior-week designations are not Week 6 statuses.','ATL','rushing_volume',1.10,['Bijan Robinson','Brian Robinson Jr.','Drake London','Caleb Williams','Luther Burden III','Rome Odunze','Michael Penix Jr.']),
'LAC@KC':('Walker-led control is the strongest early control branch','Walker is the preferred KC thesis; Chiefs DST pairing is a construction hypothesis with no numeric DST lift. Preserve Mahomes passing alternative if Chargers compete.','Official Chiefs show return from bye and Walker87 carries over4 games; Thornton IR Oct12. Chargers Week 6 media describes three rookie OL first starts in Week 5.','KC sustained rushing after rest can compress Mahomes attempts; pressured Chargers may create short fields. The volume test only moves carries, never invents sacks or turnover points.','Division familiarity, Chiefs receiver changes or Herbert success can force Mahomes to throw. Rookie OL description is evidence of change, not a calibrated pressure effect.','KC','rushing_volume',1.10,['Kenneth Walker III','Patrick Mahomes','Chiefs','Justin Herbert','Travis Kelce','Xavier Worthy','Rashee Rice']),
'NO@NYG':('An alternative passing game, led by observed receiving concentration','Winston–Nabers or Likely with Olave is an appealing secondary stack hypothesis, subject to actual Giants QB confirmation.','Current boxes link substantial Nabers/Likely targets to Giants identity and Olave/Juwan Johnson to Saints. Giants Week 6 tracker confirms matchup; no current final injury status has been captured.','If both offenses exchange drives, two concentrated receiving groups can create joint upside at lower editorial priority than Rams. This is not a claim of low public ownership.','Saints pass protection, Shough hand status, Nabers knee history and Giants QB changes can undermine efficiency. Skattebo control or a low-total grind are plausible alternatives.','NYG','passing_volume',1.10,['Jameis Winston','Malik Nabers','Isaiah Likely','Chris Olave','Tyler Shough','Cam Skattebo']),
'NYJ@NE':('Stevenson continuity is appealing; Maye remains the alternative','Stevenson and a Jets pass catcher are the early continuity idea; Maye stacks remain separate if New England attacks aggressively. Avoid carrying last week’s Hall absence forward as a fact.','League primary coverage reports Henderson expected to miss multiple weeks; Jets primary news documents Hall/Adonai inactive Week 5 and Wilson/Allen carrying much of offense.','Patriots backfield uncertainty can change concentration even without more team carries; missing complete pregame allocation means no measured Henderson-to-Stevenson transfer is emitted.','Stevenson health and Kiner participation can prevent monopoly. Jets defense generated pressure last week; that outcome does not prove identical Maye pressure or weak coverage.','NE','rushing_volume',1.10,['Rhamondre Stevenson','TreVeyon Henderson','Corey Kiner','Drake Maye','Garrett Wilson','Braelon Allen','Breece Hall']),
'PIT@TB':('Warren/Irving opportunity before a vintage-QB stack','Warren and Irving are useful opposite-side RB hypotheses; Daniels/Tez is a distinct passing alternative to evaluate after starting-QB confirmation.','Warren has carries plus receiving targets and very high Week 4 snaps. TB Oct13 official news describes Daniels second career start, Tez increasing snaps and a recent robust rushing attack.','Tampa run-led drives can keep game possessions limited while both backs accumulate use. Short passes to Warren can support him even with mediocre Steelers passing output.','Irving/Gainwell split and Steelers forcing catch-up can raise TB passing. Rodgers explosive efficiency or Daniels mobility can redirect scoring; a recent long Tez play is not a sustainable target forecast.','TB','rushing_volume',1.10,['Jaylen Warren','Bucky Irving','Kenny Gainwell','Jalon Daniels','Tez Johnson','Aaron Rodgers','DK Metcalf']),
'TEN@IND':('Taylor control; Warren as the clean passing contrast','Taylor is the first Indianapolis opportunity lean; Jones–Tyler Warren is the passing alternative. Carnell Tate/Wan’Dale are response options when Titans actually sustain drives.','Taylor observed carries/targets and Tyler Warren recent targets are substantial. Colts current reporting describes red-zone problems after Week 5; Tennessee official recap describes sluggish offense.','Indianapolis running control can accumulate Taylor work; a competitive Tennessee response instead requires more Jones passing. Regression from one red-zone failure is a hypothesis, not guaranteed TD restitution.','Titans defensive changes, Indianapolis protection or another low-efficiency finish can cap Taylor. TEN trailing volume need not produce points; rookie receiver price is not proof of value.','IND','rushing_volume',1.10,['Jonathan Taylor','Tyler Warren','Daniel Jones','Carnell Tate',"Wan'Dale Robinson",'Tony Pollard'])}
